    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d990">

                <pb facs="1117" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60i12A/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Coleman</hi>)<anchor n="13" xml:id="d990-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-30T15:00:00-05:00">January 30, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Your despatch No. 5805 and enclosed note regarding arbitration treaty.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>This Government is entirely willing to construe article I so as not to
                        require that cases be referred to the Hague Permanent Court of Arbitration
                        as long as Estonia does not become a party to the convention by which that
                        Court is established.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The Department does not understand that the Estonian Government asks that
                        the text of the article be changed.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d990-f1" n="13" type="source" xml:id="d990-f1-content">
                <p>The position of the Department as set forth in this telegram was communicated to
                    the Estonian Minister for Foreign Affairs in a note from the American Minister,
                    dated March 27, 1929; not printed (711.60i12A/16).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
